# GRADUATED out of `known_gaps/` (R49 Track H, 2026-09-03) — `todo/t0054`.
#
# Re-throwing the `catch` error-binding from inside a `match` ARM used to panic
# the Tier 2a consume-site validator at IR lowering (exit 101). It builds,
# prints 8080 and is LeakSanitizer-clean on C, LLVM and the self-host lane.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A REGRESSION NET, AND BOTH HALVES OF THE FIX ARE LOAD-BEARING —
# re-adjudicated at HEAD 2026-09-03 by breaking each in turn:
#   * no-op `ctx.set_owned(builder, err_local)` (`src/ir/lowering/exprs/mod.rs`,
#     in `lower_catch_expr`) -> the ICE RETURNS: rc 101, "Tier 2a consume-site
#     violation ... fn @handle bb6 i0 - EnumInit(Error, arg #0) - untracked
#     source consumed (ownership not decided)". So the VALUE assertion below is
#     what pins that half: without the tag the compiler does not build at all.
#   * no-op `ctx.drops.register_local(err_local, ..)` at the same site -> builds,
#     prints 8080, and leaks 2 bytes in 1 allocation. Stdout cannot see that, so
#     the ASan assertion is the half that pins it. Neither instrument covers the
#     other, which is why this fixture is wired BOTH ways.
#   * The violation text moved since filing (`bb2 i3 - AssignIntoOwnedSlot`);
#     the CLASS - untracked source consumed - is the same.
#
# The SIBLING write site is `lower_rethrow_expr`, which carries the identical
# `if matches!(err_mode, AssignMode::Move)` guard. Independent witness for the
# pair, not the fixer's own list:
#   grep -n "if matches!(err_mode" src/ir/lowering/exprs/mod.rs   -> exactly 2
# ⚠ Note when probing: both sites spell `ctx.set_owned(builder, err_local);`
# identically apart from indentation, so a substring-anchored patch silently
# hits the wrong one and reports the wrong adjudication. Anchor by LINE.
#
# The full {payload} x {nesting} axis this item promised lives in
# `catch_binding_throw_nesting_axis.gg`; this file is the ORIGINAL filed shape
# and the only cell where the recovery arm RECOVERS (8080) rather than
# re-throwing.
#
# INTENDED: `load("x")` throws `CE.NotFound("x")`; the catch binds it, the match
# takes the `NotFound` arm, the recovery value is 8080, and the heap String in
# the payload is freed.

enum CE:
    NotFound(String)
    BadPort(int)

int load(String p) throws CE:
    throw CE.NotFound(p)

int handle(String p) throws CE:
    int c = load(p)! catch (e):
        match e:
            case CE.NotFound(_):
                8080
            else:
                throw e
    return c

void main():
    print(handle("x")! catch (_): -1)
